    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Provided the parents are not sibs, their environmental deviations may be treated as independent random variables with respect to G. If, however, mates select each other on the basis of phenotypes, a correlation may exist between $ z_{f} $ and $ z_{m} $. We will denote this correlation by a. Under additive gene action, the genotypic value of an offspring is equal to the sum of the gametic contributions from its father $ (H_{f}) $ and mother $ (H_{m}) $,",
      "source_page": 839,
      "printed_page": 819,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_appendix1:p021:b7"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        58.0,
