    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Mate selection on the basis of phenotypes influences the resemblance between parents and offspring in a particularly simple manner. Perfect disassortative mating $ (a = -1) $ completely eliminates the correlation between parent and offspring phenotypes, while perfect assortative mating $ (a = +1) $ doubles it.",
